Instruction: Read the following merger agreement excerpt and answer the multiple-choice question by selecting the option that best characterizes the agreement.

Question: Is 'financial point of view' the sole consideration when determining whether a proposal qualifies as a Superior Proposal?
Option A: No
Option B: Yes

Merger Agreement Excerpt:
SECTION 8.03 – Comprehensive Proposal Evaluation. Notwithstanding any reference in Section 8.02 to Financial Criteria, the Board is required to evaluate all Acquisition Proposals by integrating both quantitative financial data and qualitative factors. In particular, prior to determining that an offer is a Superior Proposal, the Board must:
(i) Confer with its Risk Management Committee to assess potential operational and regulatory risks, in addition to standard financial modeling;
(ii) Seek an independent review from its outside legal counsel regarding compliance with applicable fiduciary standards;
(iii) Consider any strategic alignment proposals submitted concurrently by the Parent, which may include non-financial metrics such as market positioning and cultural fit;
(iv) Submit to a compliance assessment conducted by its Regulatory Affairs team.
Failure to complete any of these steps precludes the Committee from classifying the offer as a Superior Proposal. (Pages 102-104)

